		<bioghist>
			<head>2.7 Administrative History</head>
			<p>The Muslim Alliance of Indiana is a nonprofit organization dedicated to supporting the Muslim communities in Indiana through events, networking, education, and social services. They were established in 2001 shortly after the 9/11 attacks to unite Muslim Hoosiers in the face of misinformation and discrimination in America.</p>
		</bioghist>
		<scopecontent>
			<head>3.1 Scope and Content</head>
			<p>This collection documents notable services and events, including the related finances and planning, organized by nonprofit organization Muslim Alliance of Indiana (MAI). Records include meeting notes, private correspondence emails, public newsletters, event materials, financial statements, and other ephemera. Some notable events and subjects include the Governor’s Annual Iftar Dinner, annual conventions, luncheons, and legal services. This collection also includes organizational structure documents such as board member lists and details, website layout drafts, administrative records, and general informational slides and pamphlets presented at events to showcase MAI’s services and missions. Some records are related to the MAI organization but have unspecified origins or purposes.</p>
		</scopecontent>
